'''The Secret of Psalm 46''' is a talk by Brian Moriarty. Superficially, it is about video game eater eggs, encoding and finding secret messages in works of art, and puzzle hunts. But I interpret it more as a meditation on questions like: What drives people to do things (especially difficult things)? How does curiosity work? How does awe/mysterious strong driving force to make or do something work?

Tips:

* listen to this in a dark room, lying down, on headphones.

